# Pinned commit of the litlfred/folio-assistant platform.
#
# The content pipeline, the Zod schemas and every QA checker live in that repo,
# reached through the unpinned `folio-assistant/` symlink that
# scripts/setup-folio-assistant.sh creates. So every number this repo quotes —
# "run-validate: N issues", "check-wall-side: M/1190", any qa-sweep count — is a
# function of BOTH the corpus commit and the platform commit. Without a pin only
# the first is visible in `git log`, and two agents on the same corpus commit can
# measure different baselines and both be correct.
#
# That is not hypothetical: on 2026-08-08 corpus 455013fcf5 reported
# "10 issue(s)" against platform e1030e8 and "29 issue(s)" against e3c2d6b, in a
# single session, and two agents spent a round disagreeing about which baseline
# was real. Neither was wrong; the baseline was not well-defined. See bean `vbase`.
#
# Bumping the platform is TWO lines, not one, and this file used to say one.
#
# `.github/workflows/build.yml` selects the platform for the PUBLISHED build via
# its `uses:` line. That line read `@main` until 2026-09-26, so this pin governed
# only what agents measured locally while the published artifact tracked platform
# main — two platforms, one repo, no signal when they disagreed. It is now pinned
# to the same sha as the last line of this file (bean `qou-pwp9`).
#
# So when you bump: edit the sha here AND in `build.yml`, in the same commit, and
# keep them byte-identical. Checkable, so the rule is not only these comments:
#
#     bash scripts/folio-pin-coupling-check.sh      # exit 0 = the two agree
#
# It asserts only that the two LOCAL declarations agree — a drifted pair is a
# defect, an OLD pair is a choice, and it deliberately does not judge currency.
# It is NOT wired into any hook: adding one changes commit-path behaviour, which
# is the owner's call (cf. the 2026-08-25 precision hook, offered blocking and
# declined in favour of warn-only).
#
# Bumping the platform is a deliberate, reviewable edit to those two lines.
# When you bump it, state the before/after issue counts in the commit message —
# a change in count is a platform behaviour change and should be looked at, not
# absorbed silently.
#
# Override for local testing without editing this file:
#     FOLIO_ASSISTANT_REF=<branch|tag|sha> scripts/setup-folio-assistant.sh
#
